# Aggregate, cookieless traffic counting. Leave unset to disable analytics entirely.
#
# Pick one provider and set its site token. All three are cookieless and record page views
# without building a visitor profile, which is what the Privacy Policy describes.
#
#   cloudflare  Cloudflare Web Analytics. Free on any host. ID is the beacon token.
#               https://dash.cloudflare.com  ->  Analytics & Logs  ->  Web Analytics
#   plausible   ID is your site domain, e.g. vacantneu.com
#   umami       ID is the website id (a UUID)
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=cloudflare
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ID=your-token-here
#
# Only for self-hosted Plausible or Umami:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_HOST=https://analytics.example.com

# --- Engage club events (optional) ---
#
# Used by `pnpm events` in packages/scraper, not by the web app itself. Without these the
# endpoint still answers, but redacts roughly 95% of venues to "Private Location (sign in to
# display)", which is the one field this app needs.
#
# To obtain them: sign in to https://engage.northeastern.edu in a browser, then
# DevTools -> Application -> Cookies -> engage.northeastern.edu, and copy the two values.
# This is CampusGroups' own session, not Northeastern SSO, so no MFA replay is needed.
#
# Copy the values VERBATIM. The session token contains percent sequences (%2b, %3d) and
# CampusGroups expects them exactly as stored. Decoding them to "+" and "=" first yields a token
# the server does not recognise, and it does not say so: it silently issues a fresh anonymous
# session and serves every venue redacted, so the scrape looks like it worked.
#
# They expire on no published schedule. `pnpm events` exits 2 with a clear message when the
# session is refused, which it detects from the server replacing the cookie.
#
# ENGAGE_SESSION_ID=...
# ENGAGE_UID=...
